From: Surface Overdrive <noreply@surface-overdrive>
Subject: [PATCH] ipu3: eight buffers per output stream

With four, behind PipeWire one buffer was with the application, one in the software denoiser, one in the ImgU,
one waiting for the CIO2, and often none was left to queue the next request with: frames were skipped. Front
camera, 2560x1920 in good light: 19 fps through PipeWire against 31 with cam; with eight, 28 (the Camera
app's preview path the same).
---
diff --git a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
index 5abc5b9..ccc6061 100644
--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/ipu3/ipu3.cpp
@@ -163,7 +163,12 @@ private:
 class IPU3CameraConfiguration : public CameraConfiguration
 {
 public:
-	static constexpr unsigned int kBufferCount = 4;
+	/*
+	 * Buffers of each output stream. 4 were too few behind PipeWire: one with the application, one in the software
+	 * denoiser, one in the ImgU, one waiting for the CIO2, and often none left to queue the next request with, so
+	 * frames were skipped (2560x1920 in good light: 19 fps through PipeWire against 31 with cam, 2026-11-05).
+	 */
+	static constexpr unsigned int kBufferCount = 8;
 	static constexpr unsigned int kMaxStreams = 3;
 
 	IPU3CameraConfiguration(IPU3CameraData *data);
